\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{How many pairs have the same determinant?}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The links #{\qi} and #{\qj} in \ref{fdip-00ZE}
have the same individual norm differences as two copies
of #{\qi}, but only the former pair fails to commute.
The Hurwitz units of \ref{fdip-00V1} consist of signed coordinate
units and half-integer combinations of all 4 quaternion
coordinates. How do these two kinds of element determine
the values of #{s,t} in \ref{fdip-00ZD}, and how many
ordered pairs share each value?}
